Yes.  The shop keeper will come after you with a percentage chance of wanting
blood not money.  Your best bet is to a)leave the level quickly, b) Have enough
money to pay with if you are caught and lucky, c) do what I do when I have the
HP to spare and want some exp. pts.

If I have a pickaxe I make a new door from the outside, walk in and collect
as much as I can carry, take it to the doorway and drop it.  I then go back 
in and get anything else that siuts my fancy at the moment, and repeat the
manuver.  When I have what I want at the door, I make sure that my HP's are
maxed and pickup is OFF, and then - carrying NO UNPAID items - leave the shop. 
This triggers the KOPS.  If you're quick enough, you can step back into the
door and begin bashing you way back into the shop.  When you make it back in,
start trying to (p)ay for what you stole (You need to have a lot of money on
hand for this).  If your luck is still holding the shopkeeper will ease off and
allow you to try to help them recoup their losses.  The stuff in the doorway is
now yours for the taking for FREE.  BTW, This will cost you nothing; you just
need to have enough to cover the loss in your possession.

Of course, you could always wait around a convenient poly trap until your pet
has been transformed into some notably nasty demon (say a balrog :-).  He will
then kill everything that gets near him.  Just make sure that you have at least
75 HP's and a well enchanted named weapon if you have to face him in a ghost
level or get separated by a level accidently :-((((.  You MIGHT survive.

